    <section id="sobre">

        <h2>About Us</h2>

        <h3>Camile</h3>

        <h4>Birth</h4>

        <p>
                Camile Vitória Blodorn was born at 5:50 PM on January 31, 2011, at the Centro Hospitalar
                do Oeste Ltda, along with her twin brother Bruno Henrique Blodorn. She was born
                measuring 42 cm and weighing 1.675 kg. It was a moment of great joy and
                concern to see how small these two little angels were; they were
                so tiny that both of them fit into a single crib. Her older sister,
                Isabel, was eager to see her two little siblings, and she was
                absolute sure there would be two and that they would be a boy and a girl.
                They brought a lot of joy to the whole family and to the
                municipality, being one of the first sets of twin boys and girls.
        </p>


        <h4>Educational Background</h4>

        <p>
                I began my studies at age four at the Leopoldo Kuroli Municipal School,
                where I studied until the 5th grade of elementary school and finished
                in 2022. In 2023, I enrolled at the PIO XII State College, where I studied until the
                9th grade. Now, I have started High School at IFPR - Federal Institute of Paraná,
                in Toledo, an extension of the Assis Chateaubriand Campus.
        </p>


        <h4>Historical Fact:</h4>

        <p>
                My mother tells me that when I was born, there was a very intense cold spell in
                June that affected our region, recording minimum temperatures close to
                -3°C with heavy frosts, which caused one of the coldest
                mornings in recent years in the state.
        </p>


        <h4>Current Moment:</h4>

        <p>
                I believe I have evolved my knowledge and discovered a new area
                of interest. Being part of IFPR is a great opportunity,
                allowing me to meet new paths and people.
        </p>


        <h4>Future Perspectives:</h4>

        <p>
                I wish to finish high school and soon enroll in a Performing Arts
                college, where I will specialize in this field.
        </p>

    </section>


    <section id="onde-vivemos">

        <h2>Where We Live</h2>

        <h4>Municipality - Maripá:</h4>

        <p>
                    It originated on May 13, 1946, with the founding of Companhia Madeireira
                    Rio Paraná S/A (MARIPÁ). It was emancipated from Palotina by State Law
                    No. 9,226 on April 17, 1990.
                    Maripá is known for its festivals, such as the "Orchid Festival" and the "Tractor Pulling
                    Competition" (Arrancadão de Tratores), which attract people from all corners of Brazil and other
                    countries to participate. Maripá is also appreciated for its agriculture
                    and fertile soil.
        </p>


        <h4>Rural Line:</h4>

        <p>
                 It is linked to the colonization and agricultural development process
                    begun in the mid-20th century, marked by the division of small
                    rural properties and the strong presence of family farming and
                    dairy cattle ranching.
        </p>

    </section>

